 "notes": "All four planned kinds kept. Baijiu: aroma types as t (ladder from the Baijiu article); 7 archetypes (Moutai, Wuliangye, Luzhou Laojiao, Fenjiu, Erguotou, Kinmen Kaoliang, Jiugui). Old Moutai, Fen Chiew and 1573 models moved into versions where the maker matched; old 'National Cellar 1573' row kept in m as given (its maker field names the brand, not Luzhou Laojiao). Yanghe, Shui Jing Fang, Maotaizhen and small makers stay in m (no archetype source retrieved). Shochu: base and honkaku/kōrui as t; GI archetypes (Satsuma, Iki, Kuma) plus Amami kokuto, Kuro Kirishima and iichiko; duplicate Iichiko Saiten removed. Awamori: Kusu and Hanazake archetypes; old aged bottlings became kusu versions. Soju: Andong soju, Chamisul, Chum Churum, Good Day; old 'Jinro' maker renamed HiteJinro, 'Lotte Liquor' to Lotte Chilsung (as on the Soju article). Left out for lack of a retrieved page: Gujing Gongjiu, Xifeng, Jiannanchun, Hwayo, Ryukyu 1429 archetypes; founding years for Lotte Chilsung, Muhak, Beijing Hongxing. Jiugui Liquor register founding year 1956 is the Jishou Distillery root; the Jiugui brand dates from 1985."
